{"boundary":"Configured source-text signatures, not elaborated Lean or a complete dependency context. Truncation and unresolved names are explicit; full definitions and source remain on demand.","contributions":[{"author":{"kind":"agent","name":"Codex source review 2"},"body":"The exact supporting lemma is present in the source-owned canonical ingestion. The configured assertion, its definitions and the lemma construction were compared; this is an agent reading without proof replay or human approval.\n\nInspected: Read complete configured challenge including matching polytope, degree-three LocalLabels, triangleExpansion, localExtension, oldRestriction, cutMass and minFace. Independently compared pinned expansion/contraction construction, complete ex:lem-expansion-face statement and proof; the final paper sentence and proof establish minimal-face transport for an arbitrary point x, not only the uniform example.\n\nCapture rebinding by Codex, 26 October 2026: the Atlas capture revision changed after an outside-report wording correction. The pinned Lean text, configuration, paper text and proposed relation are unchanged; no new review is implied.","content_sha256":"sha256:0c4e83de658fb4ca5b7db0db091472dd174a8352d21a77cc707a97357815bc01","fingerprint":"sha256:4cfae1f7f710735b6a59c77b1c99bf91959b2897259526594c8a3b8f51692c59","kind":"statement-link","license":"Apache-2.0","navigation":{"decision":"linked","limitations":"Agent source reading; no human approval, Lean replay or whole-statement equivalence certificate. The exact supporting lemma is present in the source-owned canonical ingestion. The configured assertion, its definitions and the lemma construction were compared; this is an agent reading without proof replay or human approval.","schema":"statement-map-navigation-reading/1","source_sha256":"sha256:0b6b19f837991da8842a33f72947e2feeb595ea31f912ce2d6f607f40422391b","targets":[{"declarations":["OAI.TriangleFace198.triangle_expansion_face"],"explanation":"For a degree-three vertex in a finite loopless multigraph with a perfect matching, both statements identify the triangle-cut equality face with the original matching polytope. The extension preserves every old edge coordinate and assigns each new opposite edge its corresponding incident-edge coordinate; the lemma proof gives inverse restriction. Both preserve the uniform 1/3 point and transport its minimal face, with the formal theorem asserting the minimal-face identity for every point of the original polytope.","fingerprint":"sha256:3c9033e5bbb23a5a8e333cef22364f98b0982688b433ec5e6b2f195dbb897bb6","limitations":"The explicit all-vector inverse and coordinate identities are properties of the displayed linear extension, as described by the paper construction. This is source-level correspondence, not independent proof certification or Lean replay.","relation":"same-claim","row_id":"Entropy-and-Face-Dimension-of-the-Perfect-Matching-Polytope-September-23-2026#ex:lem-expansion-face","statement_sha256":"sha256:ebd641687de5afb317016ad2a16908d1bb6b3495e615349454e9194776b72cc7"}]},"pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","provenance":{"identity_assurance":"named local attestation; identity not independently authenticated","kind":"agent-drafted-unreviewed"},"references":["https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/lean/ComparatorChallenges/TriangleFace.lean","https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Entropy-and-Face-Dimension-of-the-Perfect-Matching-Polytope-September-23-2026/build/sections/10-examples.tex#L100","https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Entropy-and-Face-Dimension-of-the-Perfect-Matching-Polytope-September-23-2026/build/sections/10-examples.tex#L99"],"release_id":"openai-math","review_state":"unreviewed","row_id":"challenge:TriangleFace","schema":"statement-map-contribution/1"}],"detail":{"path":"lean/f4a3a9102756aedc4f93241c.json","pointer":""},"formal_statement":{"detail":{"path":"lean/f4a3a9102756aedc4f93241c.json","pointer":"/reader/formal_statement"},"full_source":{"path":"lean/f4a3a9102756aedc4f93241c.json","pointer":"/reader/formal_statement"},"kind":"declaration-signatures","method":"configured-challenge-declaration-signatures","name_resolution":"source-text","snippets":[{"complete":true,"detail":{"path":"lean/f4a3a9102756aedc4f93241c.json","pointer":"/reader/selected_statements/0"},"full_source":{"path":"lean/f4a3a9102756aedc4f93241c.json","pointer":"/challenge/lean"},"name":"OAI.TriangleFace198.triangle_expansion_face","source":{"file":"lean/ComparatorChallenges/TriangleFace.lean","line":169,"pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","sha256":"0b6b19f837991da8842a33f72947e2feeb595ea31f912ce2d6f607f40422391b","statement_sha256":"sha256:c66ed8c0b1e29bc827666a9ad13889528feec59818f5a565badab6c2b74417f4","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/lean/ComparatorChallenges/TriangleFace.lean#L169"},"text":"theorem triangle_expansion_face {V : Type uV} {E : Type uE}\n    [Fintype V] [Fintype E] [DecidableEq V] [DecidableEq E] (G : LooplessGraph V E) (v : V)\n    (hdeg : Fintype.card {e : E // G.Incident v e} = 3)\n    (_hmatching : Nonempty G.Matching) :\n    ∃ (c : E → Fin 3) (hc : LocalLabels G v c),\n      let H := triangleExpansion G c v\n      let f := localExtension G c v hc\n      let Q := {y | y ∈ H.polytope ∧ H.cutMass y (triangleVertices v) = 1}\n      f '' G.polytope = Q ∧\n      Convex ℝ Q ∧ IsExtreme ℝ H.polytope Q ∧\n      (∀ x, oldRestriction (f x) = x) ∧\n      (∀ y ∈ Q, f (oldRestriction y) = y) ∧\n      (∀ x e, f x (Sum.inl e) = x e) ∧\n      (∀ x i, f x (Sum.inr i) = x (localEdge G c v hc i)) ∧\n      (∀ x, (∀ e, x e = (1/3 : ℝ)) → ∀ e, f x e = (1/3 : ℝ)) ∧\n      (∀ x ∈ G.polytope, CanonicalFace198.minFace H.polytope (f x) = f '' CanonicalFace198.minFace G.polytope x)"}],"state":"available","unresolved_names":[]},"generation_id":